The Shell Context should hold the current state.
It includes the variables (Two different maps, for exported and non-exported shell vars),
    the current directory etc.

Mapping the ShellContext:
A shell is, by definition, an environment manipulator.
When a user runs commands like export MY_var=123 or updates their PATH,
    they expect the shell's environment to change.
Because System.getenv() is immutable, our initialization logic cannot simply hold a reference to it.

I must instantiate a new, mutable data structure (our HashMap),
    and iterate over the entries in System.getenv() and copy them into the mutable map.